WEBVTT
X-TIMESTAMP-MAP=LOCAL:00:00:00.000,MPEGTS:0

00:00.697 --> 00:05.102 align:center line:79%
The Book of Mormon concludes
with inspiring invitations for Moroni

00:05.702 --> 00:08.906 align:center line:79%
to “come unto Christ,”
“be perfected in him,”

00:09.406 --> 00:12.042 align:center line:81%
“deny [ourselves] of all ungodliness,”

00:12.476 --> 00:15.712 align:center line:79%
and “love God with all [our] might,
mind and strength.”

00:16.647 --> 00:18.515 align:center line:81%
Interestingly, the final sentence

00:18.515 --> 00:24.755 align:center line:79%
of his instruction anticipates both
the Resurrection and Final Judgment.

00:25.055 --> 00:29.660 align:center line:79%
He said, “I soon go
to rest in the paradise of God,

00:30.127 --> 00:33.297 align:center line:79%
until my spirit and body
shall again reunite,

00:33.864 --> 00:38.135 align:center line:79%
and I am brought forth
triumphant through the air, to meet you

00:38.135 --> 00:42.739 align:center line:79%
before the pleasing bar
of the great Jehovah,

00:43.307 --> 00:46.276 align:center line:81%
the Eternal Judge of both quick and dead.”

00:47.344 --> 00:50.948 align:center line:79%
I am intrigued by Moroni’s use
of the word “pleasing”

00:51.381 --> 00:53.383 align:center line:81%
to describe the Final Judgment.

00:54.117 --> 00:57.421 align:center line:79%
Other Book of Mormon prophets
likewise described the judgment as

00:57.421 --> 01:03.493 align:center line:79%
a “glorious day,” and one that we should
“look forward [to] with an eye of faith.”

01:04.328 --> 01:07.064 align:center line:81%
Yet often when we anticipate Judgment Day

01:07.531 --> 01:13.570 align:center line:79%
other prophetic descriptions come to mind,
such as “shame and awful guilt,”

01:13.971 --> 01:17.374 align:center line:81%
“dread and fear,” and “endless misery.”

01:18.775 --> 01:23.547 align:center line:79%
I believe this stark contrast in language
indicates that the doctrine

01:23.747 --> 01:25.782 align:center line:81%
of Christ enabled Moroni

01:25.782 --> 01:30.487 align:center line:79%
and other prophets to anticipate
that great day with eager

01:30.487 --> 01:32.556 align:center line:81%
and hopeful anticipation,

01:33.190 --> 01:37.461 align:center line:79%
instead of the fear they warned of
for those not spiritually prepared.

01:38.395 --> 01:40.998 align:center line:81%
What did Moroni understand

01:41.365 --> 01:43.700 align:center line:81%
that you and I need to learn?

01:44.635 --> 01:47.104 align:center line:79%
I pray for the assistance
of the Holy Ghost

01:47.437 --> 01:51.375 align:center line:79%
as we consider Heavenly Father's
plan of happiness and mercy,

01:51.942 --> 01:55.012 align:center line:79%
the Savior’s atoning role
in the Father’s plan,

01:55.579 --> 02:00.984 align:center line:79%
and how we will “be accountable for
[our] own sins in the day of judgment.”

02:02.819 --> 02:05.689 align:center line:79%
The overarching purposes
of the Father’s plan are

02:05.689 --> 02:10.794 align:center line:79%
to provide His spirit children with
opportunities to receive a physical body,

02:11.228 --> 02:15.732 align:center line:79%
learn “good from evil” through
mortal experience, grow spiritually,

02:15.966 --> 02:17.634 align:center line:81%
and progress eternally.

02:18.735 --> 02:23.974 align:center line:79%
What the Doctrine and Covenants
refers to as moral agency is central

02:23.974 --> 02:27.077 align:center line:79%
in God's plan to bring
to pass the immortality

02:27.077 --> 02:29.813 align:center line:79%
and eternal life
of His sons and daughters.

02:31.014 --> 02:35.686 align:center line:79%
This essential principle also is described
in the scriptures as agency

02:36.119 --> 02:38.722 align:center line:81%
and the freedom to choose and to act.

02:39.656 --> 02:42.959 align:center line:81%
The term “moral agency” is instructive.

02:43.860 --> 02:48.365 align:center line:79%
Synonyms for the word “moral” include
“good,” “honest,” and “virtuous.”

02:49.199 --> 02:53.937 align:center line:79%
Synonyms for the word “agency”
include “action,” “activity,” and “work.”

02:54.438 --> 03:01.144 align:center line:79%
Hence, moral agency can be understood
as the ability and privilege to choose

03:01.144 --> 03:07.384 align:center line:79%
and act for ourselves in ways
that are good, honest, virtuous, and true.

03:08.919 --> 03:13.924 align:center line:79%
God’s creations include “both things
to act and things to be acted upon,”

03:14.725 --> 03:18.395 align:center line:79%
and moral agency is the
divinely designed “power

03:18.395 --> 03:24.101 align:center line:79%
of independent action” that empowers us
as God’s children to become agents

03:24.101 --> 03:28.205 align:center line:79%
to act and not simply objects
to be acted upon.

03:30.006 --> 03:31.942 align:center line:81%
The Earth was created as a place whereon

03:31.975 --> 03:34.578 align:center line:79%
Heavenly Father’s
children could be proved

03:35.045 --> 03:38.715 align:center line:79%
to see if they would do “all
things whatsoever the Lord their God

03:38.715 --> 03:42.986 align:center line:79%
shall command them.”
A primary purpose of the creation

03:42.986 --> 03:44.721 align:center line:81%
and of our mortal existence

03:45.155 --> 03:48.225 align:center line:81%
is to provide us the opportunity to act

03:48.225 --> 03:51.795 align:center line:79%
and become what the Lord
invites us to become.

03:52.929 --> 03:57.000 align:center line:79%
The Lord instructed Enoch:
“Behold these thy brethren;

03:57.000 --> 03:59.770 align:center line:79%
they are the workmanship
of mine own hands,

04:00.337 --> 04:04.608 align:center line:79%
and I gave unto them their knowledge
in the day I created them;

04:05.175 --> 04:09.880 align:center line:79%
and in the Garden of Eden
gave I unto man his agency;

04:11.214 --> 04:15.652 align:center line:79%
and unto thy brethren have I said,
and also given commandment,

04:16.119 --> 04:20.257 align:center line:79%
that they should love one another,
and that they should choose me,

04:20.357 --> 04:21.424 align:center line:81%
their Father.”

04:22.592 --> 04:26.363 align:center line:79%
The fundamental purposes
for the exercise of agency are

04:26.363 --> 04:29.733 align:center line:81%
to love one another and to choose God.

04:30.433 --> 04:34.571 align:center line:79%
And these two purposes
align precisely with the first

04:34.571 --> 04:39.609 align:center line:79%
and second great commandments to love God
with all our heart, soul, and mind,

04:39.910 --> 04:42.612 align:center line:81%
and to love our neighbor as ourselves.

04:43.814 --> 04:49.119 align:center line:79%
Consider that we are commanded—
not merely admonished or counseled

04:50.086 --> 04:55.926 align:center line:79%
but commanded—to use our agency
to love one another and choose God.

04:55.926 --> 04:58.495 align:center line:81%
May I suggest that in the scriptures,

04:58.829 --> 05:03.400 align:center line:79%
the modifying word
“moral” is not merely an adjective,

05:03.867 --> 05:11.007 align:center line:79%
but perhaps also a divine directive
about how our agency should be used.

05:12.676 --> 05:15.712 align:center line:79%
A familiar hymn is titled
“Choose the Right” for a reason.

05:16.446 --> 05:20.350 align:center line:79%
We have not been blessed
with moral agency to do whatever we want,

05:20.417 --> 05:24.254 align:center line:79%
whenever we will. Rather,
according to the Father’s plan,

05:24.254 --> 05:28.091 align:center line:79%
we have received
moral agency to seek after

05:28.091 --> 05:30.594 align:center line:81%
and act in accordance with eternal truth.

05:31.561 --> 05:36.566 align:center line:79%
As “agents unto [ourselves],”
we should engage anxiously in good causes,

05:37.033 --> 05:41.905 align:center line:79%
“do many things of [our] own free will,
and bring to pass much righteousness.”

05:43.306 --> 05:47.677 align:center line:79%
The eternal importance of moral agency
is highlighted in the scriptural account

05:47.677 --> 05:49.112 align:center line:81%
of the premortal council.

05:50.046 --> 05:53.550 align:center line:79%
Lucifer rebelled against
the Father’s plan for His children

05:54.017 --> 05:57.354 align:center line:79%
and sought to destroy the power
of independent action.

05:57.954 --> 06:01.791 align:center line:79%
Significantly, the devil’s
defiance was focused directly

06:01.791 --> 06:04.127 align:center line:81%
on the principle of moral agency.

06:04.895 --> 06:07.297 align:center line:81%
God explained, “Wherefore,

06:07.297 --> 06:12.802 align:center line:79%
because ... Satan rebelled against me,
and sought to destroy the agency of man,

06:13.136 --> 06:15.839 align:center line:81%
... I caused that he should be cast down.”

06:17.007 --> 06:20.844 align:center line:81%
The adversary's selfish scheme was

06:20.844 --> 06:23.480 align:center line:79%
to strip away from
God's children the capacity

06:23.480 --> 06:28.151 align:center line:79%
to become “agents unto themselves,”
who could act in righteousness.

06:28.952 --> 06:32.389 align:center line:79%
His intent was to consign
Heavenly Father's children

06:32.389 --> 06:35.725 align:center line:79%
to be objects that could
only be acted upon.

06:37.727 --> 06:41.197 align:center line:79%
President Dallin H. Oaks
has emphasized that the gospel

06:41.197 --> 06:45.602 align:center line:79%
of Jesus Christ
invites us both to know something

06:46.236 --> 06:52.075 align:center line:79%
and to become something through
the righteous exercise of moral agency.

06:52.976 --> 06:58.248 align:center line:79%
He said, “Many Bible and modern
scriptures speak of a Final Judgment,

06:58.682 --> 07:03.086 align:center line:79%
at which all persons will be rewarded
according to their deeds or works,

07:03.086 --> 07:05.155 align:center line:81%
or the desires of their hearts.

07:06.356 --> 07:09.225 align:center line:79%
But other scriptures
enlarge upon this by referring

07:09.259 --> 07:13.430 align:center line:79%
to our being judged by
the condition we have achieved.

07:14.297 --> 07:18.635 align:center line:79%
The prophet Nephi describes the Final
Judgment in terms of what we have become.

07:19.669 --> 07:25.375 align:center line:79%
’And if their works have been filthiness,
they must needs be filthy;

07:25.942 --> 07:27.744 align:center line:81%
and if they be filthy

07:28.144 --> 07:31.614 align:center line:79%
it must needs be that they cannot dwell
in the kingdom of God.′

07:32.382 --> 07:38.121 align:center line:79%
Moroni declares, ’He that is filthy
shall be filthy still;

07:39.289 --> 07:43.259 align:center line:79%
and he that is righteous
shall be righteous still.’”

07:43.259 --> 07:44.961 align:center line:81%
President Oaks continued,

07:45.462 --> 07:49.833 align:center line:79%
“From such teachings we conclude
that the Final Judgment is not

07:49.833 --> 07:53.937 align:center line:79%
just an evaluation of a sum total
of good and evil acts—

07:54.270 --> 07:59.976 align:center line:79%
what we have done. It is an acknowledgment
of the final effect of our acts

07:59.976 --> 08:03.446 align:center line:81%
and thoughts—what we have become.”

08:05.515 --> 08:09.019 align:center line:79%
Our works and desires alone
do not and cannot save us.

08:09.686 --> 08:15.325 align:center line:79%
“After all we can do,” we are reconciled
with God only through the mercy

08:15.325 --> 08:18.628 align:center line:79%
and grace available
through the Savior's infinite

08:18.628 --> 08:20.797 align:center line:81%
and eternal atoning sacrifice.

08:21.831 --> 08:26.136 align:center line:79%
Alma declared, “Begin
to believe in the Son of God,

08:26.703 --> 08:28.772 align:center line:81%
that he will come to redeem his people,

08:29.305 --> 08:32.709 align:center line:79%
and that he shall suffer and die
to atone for their sins;

08:33.009 --> 08:35.945 align:center line:79%
and that he shall rise
again from the dead,

08:35.945 --> 08:38.314 align:center line:79%
which shall bring
to pass the resurrection,

08:38.915 --> 08:43.453 align:center line:79%
that all men shall stand before him,
to be judged at the last and judgment day,

08:43.653 --> 08:45.155 align:center line:81%
according to their works.”

08:46.656 --> 08:49.859 align:center line:79%
“We believe that through
the Atonement of Christ,

08:50.293 --> 08:56.466 align:center line:79%
all mankind may be saved by obedience
to the laws and ordinances of the gospel.”

08:57.634 --> 09:02.005 align:center line:81%
How grateful we should be that our sins

09:02.005 --> 09:07.143 align:center line:79%
and wicked deeds will not
stand the testimony against us if

09:07.143 --> 09:08.845 align:center line:81%
we are truly “born again,”

09:08.845 --> 09:12.148 align:center line:81%
exercise faith in the Redeemer,

09:12.549 --> 09:18.221 align:center line:79%
repent with “sincerity of heart” and
“real intent,” and “endure to the end.”

09:20.290 --> 09:23.226 align:center line:79%
Many of us may expect
that our appearance before the bar

09:23.226 --> 09:28.698 align:center line:79%
of the Eternal Judge will be similar
to a proceeding in a worldly court of law.

09:29.365 --> 09:31.334 align:center line:81%
A judge will preside.

09:31.768 --> 09:36.272 align:center line:79%
Evidence will be presented.
A verdict will be rendered.

09:36.940 --> 09:38.975 align:center line:81%
And we likely will be uncertain

09:38.975 --> 09:42.412 align:center line:79%
and fearful until we learn
the eventual outcome.

09:43.546 --> 09:47.550 align:center line:79%
But I believe such
a characterization is inaccurate.

09:48.618 --> 09:50.987 align:center line:81%
Different from but related

09:50.987 --> 09:55.592 align:center line:79%
to the mortal fears we often
experience is what the scriptures describe

09:55.592 --> 09:58.328 align:center line:79%
as “godly fear” or
the “fear of the Lord.”

09:59.295 --> 10:02.966 align:center line:79%
Unlike worldly fear
that causes alarm and anxiety,

10:03.500 --> 10:08.571 align:center line:79%
godly fear invites into our lives peace,
assurance, and confidence.

10:09.572 --> 10:12.876 align:center line:79%
Righteous fear encompasses
a deep feeling of reverence

10:12.876 --> 10:15.478 align:center line:81%
and awe for the Lord Jesus Christ,

10:15.879 --> 10:17.847 align:center line:81%
obedience to His commandments,

10:18.148 --> 10:22.785 align:center line:79%
anticipation of the final
judgment, and justice at His hand.

10:23.653 --> 10:27.891 align:center line:79%
Godly fear grows out of a correct
understanding of the divine nature

10:27.891 --> 10:29.559 align:center line:81%
and mission of the Redeemer,

10:30.260 --> 10:33.196 align:center line:79%
a willingness to submit
our will to His will,

10:33.930 --> 10:38.568 align:center line:79%
and acknowledge that every man
and woman will be accountable for his

10:38.601 --> 10:45.542 align:center line:79%
or her own mortal desires, thoughts,
words, and acts in the Day of Judgment.

10:46.776 --> 10:52.248 align:center line:79%
The fear of the Lord is not a reluctant
apprehension about coming

10:52.248 --> 10:54.317 align:center line:81%
into His presence to be judged.

10:55.218 --> 11:00.657 align:center line:79%
Rather, it is the prospect of ultimately
acknowledging about ourselves things

11:00.657 --> 11:04.727 align:center line:79%
as they really are and
as they really will be.

11:06.095 --> 11:09.332 align:center line:79%
Every person who has lived,
who does now live,

11:09.332 --> 11:11.234 align:center line:81%
and who will yet live upon the earth

11:12.035 --> 11:14.871 align:center line:79%
“shall be brought
to stand before the bar of God,

11:14.871 --> 11:17.874 align:center line:79%
to be judged of him according
to [his or her] works

11:18.274 --> 11:21.411 align:center line:79%
whether they be good
or whether they be evil.”

11:22.879 --> 11:27.116 align:center line:79%
If our desires have been for righteousness
and our works good—meaning

11:27.116 --> 11:32.322 align:center line:79%
we have exercised faith in Jesus Christ,
made and kept covenants with God,

11:32.322 --> 11:34.090 align:center line:81%
and repented of our sins—

11:34.757 --> 11:38.628 align:center line:81%
then the judgment bar will be pleasing.

11:39.729 --> 11:42.999 align:center line:79%
As Enos declared,
“We will stand before [the Redeemer];

11:43.466 --> 11:47.003 align:center line:79%
then shall [we] see
his face with pleasure,”

11:47.837 --> 11:51.274 align:center line:79%
and at the last day we will “be
rewarded unto righteousness.”

11:51.975 --> 11:57.247 align:center line:79%
Conversely, if our desires
have been for evil and our works wicked,

11:57.814 --> 12:00.817 align:center line:79%
then the judgment bar
will be a cause of dread.

12:01.718 --> 12:06.155 align:center line:79%
We will have a “perfect knowledge,”
a “bright recollection,”

12:06.155 --> 12:08.524 align:center line:81%
and a “lively sense of our own guilt.”

12:09.359 --> 12:12.228 align:center line:81%
“We shall not dare to look up to our God;

12:12.295 --> 12:17.033 align:center line:79%
and we would fain be glad
if we could command the rocks

12:17.033 --> 12:21.471 align:center line:79%
and the mountains to fall upon us,
to hide us from his presence.”

12:22.272 --> 12:26.909 align:center line:79%
And at the last day
we will “have [our] reward of evil.”

12:28.077 --> 12:32.415 align:center line:81%
Ultimately, then, we are our own judges.

12:33.049 --> 12:37.854 align:center line:79%
No one will need to tell us where
to go. In the Lord’s presence

12:37.854 --> 12:41.958 align:center line:79%
we will acknowledge what we have chosen
to become in mortality,

12:42.392 --> 12:46.296 align:center line:79%
and know for ourselves
where we should be in eternity.

12:48.097 --> 12:51.334 align:center line:79%
Understanding that the final
judgment can be pleasing is not

12:51.334 --> 12:53.569 align:center line:81%
a blessing reserved only for Moroni.

12:54.570 --> 12:58.508 align:center line:79%
Alma described promised blessings
available to every devoted disciple

12:58.508 --> 13:00.376 align:center line:81%
of the Savior. He said,

13:01.711 --> 13:07.216 align:center line:79%
“The meaning of the word restoration
is to bring back again evil for evil,

13:07.216 --> 13:13.423 align:center line:79%
or carnal for carnal, or devilish
for devilish—good for that which is good;

13:13.423 --> 13:15.525 align:center line:81%
righteous for that which is righteous;

13:15.792 --> 13:20.496 align:center line:79%
just for that which is just;
merciful for that which is merciful. ...

13:21.297 --> 13:27.036 align:center line:79%
Deal justly, judge righteously,
and do good continually;

13:27.337 --> 13:33.676 align:center line:79%
and if ye do all these things,
then shall ye receive your reward; yea,

13:33.710 --> 13:36.245 align:center line:79%
ye shall have mercy
restored unto you again;

13:36.245 --> 13:40.183 align:center line:79%
ye shall have justice
restored unto you again;

13:40.216 --> 13:45.455 align:center line:79%
ye shall have a righteous
judgment restored unto you again;

13:45.955 --> 13:49.158 align:center line:81%
and ye shall have good rewarded unto you

13:49.425 --> 13:50.426 align:center line:81%
again.”

13:51.861 --> 13:57.467 align:center line:79%
I joyfully witness that Jesus
Christ is our living Savior.

13:57.834 --> 14:03.706 align:center line:79%
Alma’s promise is true and applicable
to you and me—today, tomorrow,

14:03.706 --> 14:05.641 align:center line:81%
and for all eternity.

14:06.109 --> 14:12.382 align:center line:79%
I so testify in the sacred name
of the Lord Jesus Christ, amen.

